#X text 35 89 [display] displays messages. By default \, the number of characters is zero \, which resizes according to the input message. If you give it a fixed character number and the message is larger \, the displayed message is truncated. The object has no methods of its own: every message it gets is displayed (like [print]) and passed on. By default the display flashes when a message arrives. But you can change that via properties or creation flags. The flash time is also the display refresh rate of the object., f 82;
